只输出严格JSON，恰好包含id（metadata.id原样）、summary_zh（15到140个Unicode字符，通常40到100字）、category（枚举）、tags（2到5个不重复关键词，每个最多30字符）、confidence（0到1，仅自评）、insufficient_evidence（布尔）、evidence（1到3个对象，每个恰好包含paragraph_id、fact）、limitations（0到5个字符串）。只选择输入中长度20至120字符的完整片段编号；fact是该片段支持的中文事实转述。不要输出quote，不要自行抄写、拼接、删改或补造引用。程序会按编号附上原文。一个编号只用一次；最多3条证据。不得增加字段。
摘要和limitations保留会改变功能意义的前提、平台例外和限制：设密码后才认证、页面保持打开才提醒、依赖外部组件、估算不等于保证。只写已实现功能，不将规划当完成。证据不足就标记，不编造。
图像识别/分类不是媒体创作，没有贴切类别归other；量化、计算与领域研究归search-research，不因多智能体实现归agents-automation；模型/CLI适配与插件开发工具归coding-development；市场/精选目录按搜索发现归search-research。不要按附属同步、备份或评论功能分类。不要推断本机客户端等于本地模型。
摘要中的主要功能必须被所选片段支持。优先把改变用途含义的条件写进摘要，不能只藏在limitations。遇到“阶段1骨架”“cloud provider待实现”“匿名thread后续实现”等，摘要明确当前仅本地草稿/审批落盘，不说已实现匿名网络或云端发布。Codex/模型登录适配归coding-development；Oopz等语音房的对话连接归communication-integrations。自述兼容或性能用“作者称/README注明”，不冒充本次验证。
格式示例（仅结构，不是来源事实）：evidence:[{"paragraph_id":"p3s1","fact":"该片段支持的中文转述"}]。请从本次真实输入挑选编号。","role":"system"},{"content":"{"metadata":{"description":"Native DeepSeek Harness workbench for evidence-first vulnerability research, reproduction, and reporting.","id":"gh:1335930276","install_available":true,"language":"TypeScript","name":"dsh-omv","slug":"bx33661/dsh-omv","topics":["audit-workbench","cordis","deepseek-harness","dsh-plugin","oh-my-vul","react","security-research","security-tooling","typescript","vulnerability-assessment","vulnerability-research"]},"paragraphs":[{"id":"p1s1","text":"Native DeepSeek Harness workbench for evidence-first vulnerability research, reproduction, and repor"},{"id":"p1s2","text":"e DeepSeek Harness workbench for evidence-first vulnerability research, reproduction, and reporting."},{"id":"p2s1","text":"# OMV Audit Desk (`dsh-omv`)"},{"id":"p3s1","text":"An evidence-first vulnerability audit workbench for DeepSeek Harness, powered by the public `oh-my-v"},{"id":"p3s2","text":"nce-first vulnerability audit workbench for DeepSeek Harness, powered by the public `oh-my-vul` API."},{"id":"p4s1","text":"中文文档 · Architecture · DSH integration guide"},{"id":"p5s1","text":"Full audit desk overview: workspace summary, findings, reproduction, evidence graph, and PoC lab."},{"id":"p6s1","text":"`OMV Audit Desk` is the product name; `dsh-omv` remains the package id for upgrade compatibility. It"},{"id":"p6s2","text":" is a dual-face, native DSH bundle:"},{"id":"p7s1","text":"- a Node plugin joins DSH web-server, tool, command, system-prompt, and workspace-registry services;"},{"id":"p7s2","text":"\n- a browser client contributes a conversation view, session status, composer context, command rows,"},{"id":"p7s3","text":" settings section, and workspace launcher;\n- `cordis.patch.yml` installs both faces into a DSH Web p"},{"id":"p7s4","text":"gs section, and workspace launcher;\n- `cordis.patch.yml` installs both faces into a DSH Web profile."},{"id":"p8s1","text":"## Features"},{"id":"p9s1","text":"- Evidence-maturity dashboard with five contextual dimensions instead of a single completion percent"},{"id":"p9s2","text":"age\n- Candidate, confirmed, blocked, and archived finding ledger\n- `source → sink → guard` evidence-"},{"id":"p9s3","text":"chain inspection\n- Derived Audit Loop stages, persistent Finding-to-Session links, workflow history,"},{"id":"p9s4","text":" and Evidence diffs\n- One-click Agent workflows for audit, reproduction, deduplication, adversarial "},{"id":"p9s5","text":"review, reporting, and disclosure\n- Doctor issues, review verdicts, open questions, and exact next a"},{"id":"p9s6","text":"ctions without circular score deductions\n- Durable Campaign Runner with bounded concurrency, one nat"},{"id":"p9s7","text":"ive DSH forked session per lane, pause/resume/cancel/retry, and restart recovery\n- Provenance-aware "},{"id":"p9s8","text":"Evidence Graph, stage-aware report conditions, and structured reproduction runs\n- Closed-loop PoC la"},{"id":"p9s9","text":"boratory: editable drafts, explicit approval, Docker isolation, `/output/result.json`, artifact hash"},{"id":"p9s10","text":"es, provenance, and manual Evidence adoption\n- Dedicated quality center, reproduction lab, dedup int"},{"id":"p9s11","text":"elligence, report-readiness signals, and Campaign Graph\n- DSH-native visual system that uses the hos"},{"id":"p9s12","text":"t background layers, borders, typography, and alias colors directly, with calm hierarchy, sticky wor"},{"id":"p9s13","text":"kbench chrome, and responsive mobile breakpoints\n- Campaign outcomes distinguish completed work from"},{"id":"p9s14","text":" blocked lanes that still need attention\n- Campaign compatibility diagnostics isolate malformed YAML"},{"id":"p9s15","text":", normalize common registry aliases, and repair derived metadata from the workbench\n- Workspace-wide"},{"id":"p9s16","text":" search, recent activity feed, and native DSH Job status with contextual repair-and-retry\n- SSE work"},{"id":"p9s17","text":"space synchronization with polling fallback\n- Recent workspace activity surfaced on the overview pag"},{"id":"p9s18","text":"e\n- Candidate creation, validation, reproduction scaffolding, promotion, and restore actions\n- 29 mo"},{"id":"p9s19","text":"del tools covering workspace quality, DSH lifecycle diagnostics, Finding, workflow, Campaign Runtime"},{"id":"p9s20","text":", evidence provenance, reproduction, PoC isolation, dedup, and search\n- 19 durable `/omv*` commands,"},{"id":"p9s21","text":" including `omv-dedup` and the Campaign Runtime set\n- Automatic binding to the current DSH session w"},{"id":"p9s22","text":"edup` and the Campaign Runtime set\n- Automatic binding to the current DSH session workspace\n[该节后续省略]"},{"id":"p10s1","text":"## Install"},{"id":"p11s1","text":"There are two separate installation steps: `npm install` prepares this checkout's dependencies and b"},{"id":"p11s2","text":"uild output; `dsh plugin --profile web add ...` installs the plugin into the DSH Web profile. Choose"},{"id":"p11s3","text":" one of the following modes."},{"id":"p12s1","text":"### Source development (recommended for UI work)"},{"id":"p13s1","text":"Use a local link when you need hot reload. The link points the profile at this checkout, while `npm "},{"id":"p13s2","text":"run dev` watches `src/` and lets DSH client-HMR refresh the open page."},{"id":"p14s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p15s1","text":"Keep `npm run dev` running while editing. React component state may reset according to DSH HMR behav"},{"id":"p15s2","text":"ior; this is not full page-state persistence. If the profile previously used a regular local install"},{"id":"p15s3","text":", switch it explicitly:"},{"id":"p16s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p17s1","text":"### Stable local install"},{"id":"p18s1","text":"Use this mode when you want to run a fixed checkout without hot reload. After source changes, rebuil"},{"id":"p18s2","text":"d and add the local package again."},{"id":"p19s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p20s1","text":"### Packed install"},{"id":"p21s1","text":"Use a tarball to transfer or install a specific build on another machine. `npm pack` prints a versio"},{"id":"p21s2","text":"ned filename; use the actual filename it prints. A tarball does not provide source hot reload."},{"id":"p22s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p23s1","text":"Local checkouts and already-built tarballs do not need an extra pnpm `allowBuilds` entry. Update an "},{"id":"p23s2","text":"installed package with `dsh plugin --profile web update dsh-omv`, or remove it with `dsh plugin --pr"},{"id":"p23s3","text":"ofile web remove dsh-omv`."},{"id":"p24s1","text":"The **Vulnerability audit** entry opens or reuses the configured DSH Workspace. Every session then e"},{"id":"p24s2","text":"xposes a **Vulnerability audit** tab beside Chat and Trajectory. Verify the profile after installati"},{"id":"p24s3","text":" **Vulnerability audit** tab beside Chat and Trajectory. Verify the profile after installation with:"},{"id":"p25s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p26s1","text":"The output should include the `dsh-omv` configuration layer. If source changes do not appear, confir"},{"id":"p26s2","text":"m that the profile uses `link:.` and that `npm run dev` is still running."},{"id":"p27s1","text":"## Security model"},{"id":"p28s1","text":"- By default the API is loopback-only: the client address must be `127.0.0.1`/`::1` and the `Host` h"},{"id":"p28s2","text":"eader must be `localhost`/`127.0.0.1`/`[::1]`. The Host check blocks browser DNS-rebinding pages fro"},{"id":"p28s3","text":"m reading `/export` or forging `/action` mutations.\n- **`allowRemoteAccess: true` disables both guar"},{"id":"p28s4","text":"ds, and the whole API (including every mutation action) has no authentication.** Only enable it on a"},{"id":"p28s5","text":" trusted network, behind your own auth proxy or network isolation.\n- Local access through a non-loop"},{"id":"p28s6","text":"back hostname (for example a custom hosts domain) also requires `allowRemoteAccess: true` to pass th"},{"id":"p28s7","text":" (for example a custom hosts domain) also requires `allowRemoteAccess: true` to pass the Host check."},{"id":"p29s1","text":"Other plugins can consume the host capability without depending on the HTTP bridge:"},{"id":"p30s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p31s1","text":"See README.zh-CN.md for architecture, API, packaging, and configuration details.\nThe implementation-"},{"id":"p31s2","text":"to-guide checklist and follow-up iterations live in DSH-INTEGRATION.md."}],"truncated":true}","role":"user"}],"model":"MiniMax-M3.1-Flash","reasoning_effort":"low","stream":false}
